 GKW
=====

This file contains a brief overview of the package contents and instruction on building the code.
For more details, please see the CPC article associated with the code.

 Quick start
=============

  1) [if necessary] Edit the src/makefile file to correspond with your compilers etc.
  2) run make [from this directory]
  you should then have the executable gkw.x in this directory

  
  To use the GNU compiler to produce an executable capable of running the simple example
  (WITHOUT modifying the makefile) :

  1) make FC=gfortran FFLAGS="-O2" FFTLIB=nofft PARALLEL=nompi LDFLAGS=""

  You can always run `make clean' to start again.
  
 SAMPLES
=========

The samples/ directory contains various example input files. Details of each example can
be found in the input files (input.dat) themselves.

 SIMPLE EXAMPLE
================

We provide a simple example which should work without any FFT library or MPI.
This example may not be very meaningful -- it can be seen as a test case.

1) go to the samples/simple_example directory
2) run `gkw.x' e.g. ../../gkw.x if you followed the makefile build above

You should get something like this to standard output:
---------------------------------------------------------

 Running on            1  processors


 With mode_box off input value of krhomax is ignored
 No 2D diagnostics will be written
 Ensure you have            1  value(s) in kthrho list


 Maximum linear timestep estimate:  1.16974E-02
 Input timestep:                    1.00000E-02
 Fields timestep estimate  currently disabled

Time step :    30 Normalised time :   3.00000E-01
nMode   1 xMode   1 Growth rate  -2.82785E+00
nMode   1 xMode   1 Real frequency   2.89927E+00
Toroidal mode   1 Radial mode   1 Species  1
The particle flux  (ES/EM) :   5.93953E-18   0.00000E+00
The energy flux    (ES/EM) :  -3.46472E-03   0.00000E+00
The momentum flux  (ES/EM) :   3.75950E-19   0.00000E+00

...
...
...

Time step :  1500 Normalised time :   1.50000E+01
nMode   1 xMode   1 Growth rate   1.84496E-01
nMode   1 xMode   1 Real frequency   6.64236E-01
Toroidal mode   1 Radial mode   1 Species  1
The particle flux  (ES/EM) :  -1.85408E-17   0.00000E+00
The energy flux    (ES/EM) :   4.47490E-03   0.00000E+00
The momentum flux  (ES/EM) :  -3.06542E-20   0.00000E+00


 Run succesfully completed, Run time :   39.125000000000000
                     (main loop time):   38.500000000000000 
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You should end up with various output files, a *reference* copy of which can be found in the
output/ directory.

The energy flux (col2 in fluxes.dat) should reach around 4.47E-3 and the growth rate
(col2 in time.dat) should be around 1.8E-1.

In order to restart the run, you can clean up the output files by running ../../bin/gkw_clean_run

 CONTENTS
==========

README : this file

makefile : top level makefile which runs `make' in src/

src/
    (all Fortran source code files, other than the makefile)

        collisionop.F90      : the collision operator part of the linear terms
        functions.F90        : some wrappers for simple functions used in the code
        linear_terms.F90     : linear terms
        non_linear_terms.F90 : non linear terms
        components.F90       : species related data
        general.F90          : some routines which have no special place
        makefile             : the makefile
        normalise.F90        : normalization
        constants.f90        : some constants
        geom.F90             : geometry
        marsaglia.f90        : KISS random number generator of George Marsaglia for initial condition
        rotation.F90         : rotation/shearing related things
        control.F90          : main control switches
        global.F90           : global parameters/variables
        matdat.F90           : builds/sorts/compresses a matrix for (primarily) linear terms
        specfun.f90          : some modified routines from the specfun library
        diagnostic.F90       : most of the code outputs
        grid.F90             : grid sizes
        mode.F90             : 
        dist.F90             : main arrays and index functions
        init.f90             : initialisation related
        mpicomms.f90         : contains some additional MPI communicators
        velocitygrid.F90     : velocity space grid options
        exp_integration.F90  : expilicit integrations; field update
        io.F90               : file related
        mpidatatypes.F90     : some derived MPI datatypes
        fft.F90              : interface to FFTW3 (and others)
        linart.f90           : main program
        mpiinterface.F90     : various MPI routines

samples/
	 
	(each subdirectory contains an input file detailing what it does)
 
        cyclone/         : a nonlinear cyclone case
        general/         : documents all the possible switches used in the code
        minimal/         : a minimal input file
        simple_example/  : a small linear case based on cyclone
        simple_itg/      : a small ITG case that can be run on 1 processor
        STD/             : Waltz standard case
        STD_kinetic/     : kinetic Waltz standard case

bin/

     gkw_clean_run : Script to remove the output files from the local run directory in order to start
                    a new run.
     gkw_construct-parallel-output.sh : Post processing script to reconstruct parallel.dat output for
                                       runs with parallel s grid.
     gkw_construct-parallel-output.pl : a Perl version of the above file, which is much faster for
	                                   large files.

